{"slug":"mike-rogers-michigan-politician","qid":"Q970515","name":"Mike Rogers","desc":"American politician (born 1963)","article":"Mike Rogers (Michigan politician)","born":"1963-06-02","died":null,"birthplace":"Livingston County","parties":["Republican Party"],"offices":[{"t":"U.S. Representative","w":"MI-08","f":2001,"u":2015},{"t":"State Senate of Michigan","w":"","f":1995,"u":2001}],"summary":"Michael Joseph Rogers (born June 2, 1963) is an American politician and former Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) agent who from 2001 to 2015 was the U.S. representative for Michigan's 8th congressional district. A member of the Republican Party, he chaired the United States House Permanent Select Committee on Intelligence from 2011 to 2015.\nRogers was the Republican nominee in the 2024 U.S. Senate election in Michigan, losing narrowly to Democrat Elissa Slotkin.","photo":{"f":"mike-rogers-michigan-politician.jpg","by":"P.J. Siquig","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mike_Rogers_in_November_2019_(3x4_cropped).jpg"},"history":[{"y":2026,"o":"S","k":"MI-SEN","p":"R","n":"Mike Rogers","race":"MI-SEN"},{"y":2024,"o":"S","k":"MI","p":"R","v":2693680,"s":48.3,"w":false,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2012,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":202217,"s":58.6,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2010,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":156931,"s":64.08,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2008,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":204408,"s":56.53,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2006,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":157237,"s":55.27,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2004,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":207925,"s":61.03,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2002,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":156525,"s":67.88,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"},{"y":2000,"o":"H","k":"MI-08","p":"R","v":145179,"s":48.79,"w":true,"n":"Mike Rogers"}]}